  "description": "Callback frame codec cases (4-byte big-endian length + UTF-8 JSON body, 64 KiB body cap). Each case feeds `chunks` in order to a fresh decoder created with `maxFrameBytes`; `expect` is the outcome after the last chunk: `payloads` (decoded JSON values, in order) plus `pendingBytes` (bytes buffered that do not yet form a frame, default 0), or `error` (\"too-large\" when a header exceeds the cap, rejected before any body is buffered; \"malformed\" when a body is not valid JSON). A chunk is a lowercase hex string, or {\"jsonStringFrame\": N}: one complete frame whose body is a JSON string of N \"a\" characters. A payload may likewise be {\"jsonString\": N}. The TypeScript test (src/shared/callback/protocol.test.ts) and the Go mirror must agree on every case.",
